{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/45303-share-your-music-scores","id":45303,"title":"Share your Music Scores!","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-01-08T19:39:11-08:00","id":45303,"title":"Share your Music Scores!","content":"The World of Darkness... What else there is to say other than &quot;Music For The Masses.&quot;<br /> i made this little thread not to share specific songs, but albums and soundtracks for the WoD<br /> <br /> Ghosts by NIN its an amazing album that works perfectly on any setting. funny enough i been fiddling with the idea of a group of masked serial killers (Euthanathos) and the score on their game would be mainly the one of Drive and Hotline Miami.<br /> <br /> As for other games, i usually go fo the &quot;Pi&quot; and &quot;Fight Club&quot; score, also &quot;The Girl With The Dragon Tatto.&quot; has an amazing feel for the WoD","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-08T21:15:05-08:00","id":45369,"title":"","content":"A friend of mine once called Oingo Boingo's <i>Dead Man's Party</i> album &quot;World of Darkness: The Musical.&quot; While it may fit the nWoD marginally better (Weird Science is just such a perfect theme song for Promethean), it still nails things pretty well.<br /> <br /> I'm also pissed that you beat me to suggesting the Hotline Miami soundtrack. I've had <i>Silver Lights</i> in my head as the thing to play once a group of Wraiths first have their Cauls removed and are faced with the Shadowlands for at least a week now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-09T04:01:06-08:00","id":45494,"title":"","content":"I've mentioned it elsewhere but one of my favorites is the the movie score of the first The Crow movie by Greame Revell. For Dark and Broody I have a playlist of many obscure movie scores, but The Crow score is quintessential World of Darkness to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/31/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><a href=\"http://glyphery.webs.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ut0SZ4h.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1332-darling_rose","name":"Darling_Rose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1332_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-10T14:38:20-08:00","id":46506,"title":"","content":"The PCs had just carjacked a black luxury SUV while trying to flee from Oakland's Scourge when I ended the session for the night. Next session, we opened at the beginning of the car chase which followed. This is what was playing on the SUV's overkill sound system:<br /> <br /> Coolio - Gansta' Paradise<br /> Limp Bizkit - Rollin (Urban Assault Vehicle)<br /> Jedi Mind Tricks - The Philosophy Of Horror<br /> Ludacris - Act a Fool (DirtyVersion)<br /> DMX - Fuck Y'all<br /> N.W.A. - 100 Miles And Runnin'<br /> Helmet &amp; House Of Pain - Just Another Victim<br /> DMX - Ruff Ryders' Anthem<br /> Jay-Z - Brooklyns Finest<br /> Jedi Mind Tricks - The Worst<br /> N.W.A - Straight Outta Compton<br /> Public Enemy - Welcome To The Terrordome<br /> Anthrax &amp; Public Enemy - Bring The Noise<br /> Westside Connection - Gangsta Nation<br /> Little Brother - Speed Racing<br /> Jay Z - Big Pimpin'<br /> <br /> Special thanks for this mix go out to several contributors on the old WW forum, who gave me a number of good suggestions for rap artists and songs to check out. This is is far from a general-purpose WoD soundtrack, but it was perfect for the setting and scene of this game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800000\"><b>Demon Cat</b></span><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://flamingporcupine.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Illuminated Dark Ages character sheets and more</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10-demon-cat","name":"Demon Cat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avata